# GoPro Video Sorting

This project analyzes GoPro videos from a folder and classifies timeline segments into:

- `movement`
- `stationary`
- `night`

It produces a single unified timeline across all videos in the folder and exports practical files for review and editing.

## Features

- Folder scan for common video formats (`.mp4`, `.mov`, `.mkv`, `.avi`)
- Start-time inference from GoPro filename pattern like `20220304T000819S000000_GH580049.MP4`
- Night detection based on frame brightness
- Large-motion detection based on optical flow (smoothed to avoid small jitter noise)
- Unified timeline sorted by absolute start time across all videos
- Export outputs:
	- `timeline.csv`
	- `timeline.json`
	- `summary.json`
	- `cut_by_label.sh` (ready-to-run ffmpeg cut commands)

## Project Structure

```text
src/gopro_sorting/
	__init__.py
	config.py
	models.py
	discovery.py
	analyze_brightness.py
	analyze_motion.py
	classify.py
	timeline.py
	exporters.py
	edit_script.py
	cli.py
	gui.py
tests/
	conftest.py
	test_discovery.py
	test_timeline.py
	test_exporters.py
$RESEARCHSAMPLES/gopro_video_sorting/
	20220304T000819S000000_GH580049.MP4
```

The repository lives inside a flat project repository:

```text
gopro_video_sorting/
	gopro_video_sorting/   # git repository
	$RESEARCHSAMPLES/gopro_video_sorting/       # small local sample videos
	$RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/             # generated timelines, summaries, and clip scripts
```

## Requirements

- Linux
- Python 3.11+
- `ffmpeg` installed in PATH (for clip cutting/rearranging workflow)

Install Python dependencies:

```bash
uv sync
```

## Run: CLI

From repository root:

```bash
uv run python -m gopro_sorting.cli $RESEARCHDATA --output-dir $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting
```

Optional tuning:

```bash
uv run python -m gopro_sorting.cli $RESEARCHDATA \
	--output-dir $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting \
	--brightness-night-threshold 40 \
	--motion-threshold 2.2 \
	--sample-every-n-frames 30 \
	--min-segment-seconds 3.0 \
	--confidence-floor 0.55 \
	--max-analysis-seconds 120
```

## Run: GUI

```bash
uv run python -m gopro_sorting.gui
```

Pick input/output folders and click `Run analysis`.

## Output Files

- `$RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/timeline.csv`
	- Spreadsheet-friendly timeline of all segments.
- `$RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/timeline.json`
	- Structured version of the timeline.
- `$RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/summary.json`
	- Durations by class and low-confidence segment list.
- `$RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/cut_by_label.sh`
	- Shell script containing ffmpeg commands to cut each segment into:
		- `$RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/clips/movement/`
		- `$RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/clips/stationary/`
		- `$RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/clips/night/`

## How to Cut Videos by Type

After generating output files:

```bash
$RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/cut_by_label.sh
```

This creates per-segment clips organized by class.

## How to Rearrange Videos by Type

Example: create one ordered list with `night` clips first, then `stationary`, then `movement`.

```bash
find $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/clips/night -type f -name '*.mp4' | sort > $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/night.list
find $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/clips/stationary -type f -name '*.mp4' | sort > $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/stationary.list
find $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/clips/movement -type f -name '*.mp4' | sort > $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/movement.list
cat $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/night.list $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/stationary.list $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/movement.list > $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/reordered.list
```

Convert into ffmpeg concat format:

```bash
awk '{print "file '\''" $0 "'\''"}' $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/reordered.list > $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/concat.txt
```

Render one merged playback video:

```bash
ffmpeg -y -f concat -safe 0 -i $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/concat.txt -c copy $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/reordered_merged.mp4
```

If stream-copy concat fails due to codec differences, re-encode:

```bash
ffmpeg -y -f concat -safe 0 -i $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/concat.txt -c:v libx264 -c:a aac $RESEARCHOUTPUT/gopro_video_sorting/reordered_merged_reencoded.mp4
```

## Threshold Tuning Tips

- Too many clips labeled `movement`:
	- Increase `--motion-threshold`.
- Movement missed during strong ship/camera movement:
	- Decrease `--motion-threshold`.
- Too many clips labeled `night`:
	- Decrease `--brightness-night-threshold` sensitivity by lowering threshold value.
- Night not detected enough:
	- Raise `--brightness-night-threshold`.

## Tests

```bash
uv run pytest -q
```

## Notes

- Filename timestamp parsing assumes UTC for GoPro-style names.
- If filename pattern is missing, file modification time is used as fallback for timeline ordering.
